.TH CLIGRID 1 "September 2026" "Cli Griderator"
.SH NAME
cligrid \- persistent GTK3 and VTE terminal grid
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cligrid
.RI [ verb " [arguments]]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start or raise a grid of persistent tmux terminals. Six panes are shown by
 default; one to twenty panes are supported. Sessions survive hiding,
restarting, quitting and crashes. Reset and run-all replace sessions.
.SH COMMANDS
Pane numbers are one-based. Optional pane numbers refer to the focused pane.
Use help for command argument details in the installed version.
.PP
Commands that end sessions, drop panes or close the window (reset, all,
remove, quit and their aliases) are refused when the request comes from a
process running inside one of the grid's own panes, such as a coding agent,
unless
.B \-\-force
follows the verb, as in
.BR "cligrid reset \-\-force 2" .
Set
.B guard
to
.B off
in the configuration to turn this off. Every other command is unaffected.
.TP
.B show, raise
Show the window.
.TP
.B hide
Hide the window without ending sessions.
.TP
.B toggle
Minimize or restore the window.
.TP
.B zoom [N|off]
Fill the window with one pane, or restore the grid.
.TP
.B panes N, windows N
Set the pane count, from 1 to 20.
.TP
.B remove [N], close-window [N]
Remove a pane from the grid.
.TP
.B restart [N]
Reconnect the pane while keeping its session.
.TP
.B reset [N], fresh [N], new [N]
End and replace the selected session, or all sessions when no pane is given.
.TP
.B all command, fill command, run-all command
Replace all pane sessions with the specified command.
.TP
.B fit
Reapply the configured window fit.
.TP
.B focus N
Focus pane N.
.TP
.B swap A B
Exchange the panes at positions A and B.
.TP
.B status
Show status; output is JSON when piped or when requested with --json.
.TP
.B quit
Exit the grid while keeping tmux sessions running.
.TP
.B send
Send text to a pane.
.TP
.B run
Run a command in a pane.
.TP
.B dump N [\-\-lines K]
The last K lines of a pane (default 40). A tmux pane is read through
tmux, so scrollback is included; any other pane gives what is on screen.
.TP
.B wait N \-\-until PATTERN [\-\-timeout SECONDS]
Wait for a pane output pattern, with a timeout. The pattern is a regular
expression of at most 256 characters, matched against the pane's last rows.
.TP
.B events [\-\-kinds a,b] [\-\-since SEQ]
Stream recorded events as JSON lines, optionally filtered by kind and
replayed from a sequence number. A client that stops reading is
disconnected once it holds a megabyte of unread events.
.TP
.B watch
Follow events; the same as events.
.TP
.B help
Show command help. Also available as --help.
.TP
.B ws, workspace
List, select or manage saved workspaces.
.TP
.B layout [name | \-\-list]
Select the grid layout, or list the shapes.
.TP
.B stack A B ..., stack \-\-clear
Put panes in one cell as tabs, or undo every stack.
.TP
.B theme
Select the theme.
.TP
.B doctor
Report Python, GTK/VTE, tmux, font, configuration, icons, launcher,
desktop entry, runtime directory and desktop session checks with suggested fixes.
.TP
.B rename
Rename a pane.
.TP
.B move
Move a pane.
.TP
.B palette
Open the command palette.
.TP
.B find
Search terminal output.
.TP
.B log [K]
The last K lines of the window's log (default 40).
.TP
.B notify text
Show the text as a toast in the grid and as a desktop notification.
.TP
.B keymap
The active shortcuts and the actions they can run, as JSON.
.TP
.B state
Show pane activity states.
.TP
.B version
Show the application version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cligrid/config.json
Settings, created on first change. Defaults include maximized fit,
JetBrainsMono Nerd Font at 11 points, six panes and tmux sessions g1 through g6.
Schema 2 stores named workspaces and global preferences.
.B guard
is
.B panes
by default; see COMMANDS.
.TP
.I ~/.config/cligrid/state.json
The last arrangement: pane order, active pane, zoom, layout and stacks.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/cligrid.log
The window's log, trimmed to its last 256 KB at each launch.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf
Terminal preferences (padding, copy-on-select) and, when the theme setting is
kitty, the terminal colours. The grid otherwise uses its own palette.
.TP
.I ~/bin/cligrid
User launcher created by install.sh; invokes the application copied to
~/.local/share/cligrid, so the checkout or extract can be removed afterwards.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/cligrid.desktop
Desktop application entry. A desktop copy is installed at ~/Desktop/cli-griderator.desktop.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor
Scalable and pixel-sized application icons.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration root; defaults to ~/.config.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Socket directory; defaults to /tmp.
.TP
.B CLIGRID_WORKSPACE
Workspace name used when migrating a legacy configuration.
.TP
.B CLIGRID, CLIGRID_SLOT
Set to 1 and the pane number in every pane's environment. The guard reads
CLIGRID from a client process to tell a request from inside the grid.
.TP
.B CLIGRID_SOCKET
Full path of the control socket, for a second grid beside the first.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable terminal colors. Diagnostic reports are always plain text.
.SH INSTALLATION
Run bash install.sh from any directory. No network access is needed.
The optional --prefix DIRECTORY replaces the home-directory installation root.
The installer refuses root and skips files whose contents and modes are correct.
Icon rendering uses system Python, PyGObject and GdkPixbuf with SVG support.
The Debian builder is packaging/build-deb.sh; its package installs under /usr.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR fc-match (1)
